    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2REPu5rd658cVCXeBZEf9he)_\n\n## Merge order\n- Base: `main`, which already contains #415 (merged 2026-11-14). It touches only `sp-devonthink-browse` (one line in `sp-devonthink-record-pdf`) and `sp-academic` (one `require`).\n- Independent of #418–#421, #451 and #452; a merge conflict is unlikely, and if there is one it is a one-line `require`/README row.\n- If merged before the others: nothing breaks. If merged after: nothing breaks either.\n\n## What\n- New module `sp-pdf-reader` (`docs/tangles/academic/sp-pdf-reader.org`):\n  - `use-package emureader :ensure t` (GNU ELPA through Elpaca; no hand-cloned checkout).\n  - `sp-pdf-open FILE &optional PAGE`: opens in emureader at a PDF page (from 1); falls back to `find-file` with a message when emureader is not installed or built.\n  - The three emureader functions used are variables (`sp-pdf-reader-function-open`, `-goto-page`, `-build`).\n- `sp-devonthink-record-pdf` (Embark `p`) now calls `sp-pdf-open`.\n- Required from `sp-academic`; README row added.\n- Annotations are unchanged and stay in DEVONthink: emureader only views (no highlights or annotations).\n\n## Not verified\n- emureader 0.4.0 on GNU ELPA is the renamed `emacs-reader`. Its source could not be read from the cloud container, so `emureader-open-doc`, `emureader-goto-page` and `emureader-build` are assumed from the old `reader-*` names. If one is wrong, set the matching `sp-pdf-reader-function-*` variable.\n- 4 ERT tests pass (dispatch and fallback, with the reader stubbed) and the browse tests still pass (8); nothing was run against the real module.\n\n## Manual testing\nMac, `~/.config/emacs-modular`. emureader needs `brew install mupdf gcc make`.\n- [ ] Check out: `cd ~/dotfiles; git fetch origin 453-emureader-pdf-reader; git checkout 453-emureader-pdf-reader`, restart Emacs (Elpaca installs emureader).\n- [ ] `M-x emureader-build` works (if the command name is wrong, see `M-x apropos emureader-build` and set `sp-pdf-reader-function-build`).\n- [ ] `M-: (list (fboundp 'emureader-open-doc) (fboundp 'emureader-goto-page))` → `(t t)`.\n- [ ] `M-x sp-pdf-open` on a PDF → opens in emureader; `C-u M-x sp-pdf-open`, page 5 → opens at page 5.\n- [ ] `C-c k d b`, Embark `p` on a record → the PDF opens in emureader.\n- [ ] Without emureader built, Embark `p` → message \"emureader is not ready\", PDF opens with `find-file`.\n- [ ] `M-x sp-devonthink-highlight` (annotations in DEVONthink) still works as before.\n- [ ] Delete `var/elpaca/sources/emacs-reader` (old checkout) and restart: nothing complains.\n- [ ] Unit tests: `cd ~/.config/emacs-modular; emacs -Q --batch -L libraries/modules/academic -l ert -l tests/sp-pdf-reader-test.el -f ert-run-tests-batch-and-exit` → 4 pass.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9WVc3ZxBjNArViRDW)_",
